{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Consecutive section references are a cited ticket format, and dropping the second can allow success without assessing its requirements."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A heading inside a collapsed details block can truncate a referenced section and leave later requirements unchecked."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A prose sentence mentioning a section can add unintended requirements and send an otherwise complete run to human review."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The specified regression cases are missing, although the adjudicators identified no corresponding runtime defect."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"The reproduced diff audit flags the fixture as a skipped test and blocks delivery during the normal audit."}]}